WEBVTT

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:10.910
Shimamura is just Shimamura.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:14.750
And she'll always probably
just be Shimamura in my heart.

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:19.290
I don't really get it,
but there's just a peace of mind.

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:22.080
Something that just gets my guard down.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:25.040
It's a wonderful thing.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:28.620
Shukoh... Shukoh...

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:31.080
Ah, so you did show up again today.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:32.870
And who might this be?

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:35.830
She is <i>the </i>Shimamura.

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:37.330
What does that even mean?

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:40.080
Oho... So you're...

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:42.410
So, uh... What's your name?

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:48.000
Unlike my foolish compatriot,
I have come prepared with a name!

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.950
Please call me Yashiro Chikama.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:54.370
I've come to Earth in search of my compatriot.

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:56.910
Compatriot...?

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:31.660
Compatriot? Oh, compatriot. Like a friend?

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:33.950
Wait, there's more of you?

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:36.370
Or rather, did you just say "Earth"?

00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:39.910
My compatriot came to this planet on a mission,

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:42.290
but they haven't been back ever since.

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:45.160
So I had no choice but to search for them,

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:47.790
but it appears that I have landed
in the wrong location.

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:49.790
Alrighty, Shimamura.

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:54.450
You go ahead and enjoy talking
about the unknown with them.

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:55.290
What?!

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:58.370
Aha! I sense some fishies over there!

00:02:58.370 --> 00:02:59.250
Hey!

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:00.450
Sneaky, sneaky, sneak.

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:05.750
Curse you, Hino. So the real reason
you invited me fishing was...

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:10.870
So I hear that your name is Shimamura.

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:14.040
Huh? Uh... yeah.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:19.200
I hear that you're so popular that all
the locals come in droves to see you.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:21.370
Yeah, I'm definitely not that Shimamura.

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:23.160
Ah, such modesty.

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:28.370
Oh, I have come from the future,
so I am not a local.

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:29.620
Just so we're clear.

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:34.330
Sure, and I've come from the past.
Nice to meet you.

00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:36.870
You seem to be a typical earthling.

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:38.620
Yeah, I guess.

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:42.500
Why don't you take that thing off?

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:46.540
My face is not quite ready,
so I do ask for your patience.

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:50.330
What? Is your face going to be delivered
from the bread factory or something?

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:56.580
Shouldn't you be looking for your friend,
or rather, your compatriot?

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:59.790
Well, I'm hungry...

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:01.290
Is this something philosophical?

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:05.080
I have already confirmed
that my compatriot is safe,

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:07.750
so I figured I would take it easy.

00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:09.830
So they contacted you?

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:12.410
Well, something like that.

00:04:12.410 --> 00:04:15.620
If you're able to contact each other,
you can probably find each other...

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:18.040
And there is a reason that we cannot!

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:19.160
--Shukoh... Shukoh...

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:21.450
--I-I see.
--Shukoh... Shukoh...

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:22.500
Plop.

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:28.620
I can't seem to get a bite.

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:32.000
It's important that you realize that first...

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.080
Uh-huh...

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:36.040
You can't seem to get a bite.
Things aren't going as planned.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:40.370
But that basically means
that you've started something.

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:48.830
You just felt like doing that?

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:50.410
Fishy!

00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:51.910
Heck yeah!

00:04:54.830 --> 00:05:00.250
All we can do from here
is wish for a bright future,

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:02.700
and cast our lines.

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:09.040
So, yeah... That happened.

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:10.580
Huh.

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:11.950
Was I that boring?

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:14.080
Not exactly.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.620
Could you not say it like that?

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:18.500
Sorry, my bad.

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:20.120
Are you tired?

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:23.000
Well, I was pretty busy
at work yesterday.

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:26.750
Wait, you have a part-time job
somewhere? Where?

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:29.450
I'm not telling you.

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:31.500
Why, though?

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:33.870
Because you'd probably show up if I did.

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:35.120
Well, yeah.

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:39.160
No, it's embarrassing.

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:41.330
But it's not.

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:43.910
The fact that you're working is admirable.

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:49.080
Adachi once said that I was like a cat.

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:53.950
The fact that I keep my distance from others
makes me cat-like, apparently.

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:58.160
Though there is a part of me
that doesn't want to open up to people.

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:03.250
But Adachi's basically the same.

00:06:04.370 --> 00:06:09.500
Adachi dozing off with her head on my lap
definitely reminded me of a cat.

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:15.910
What is it?

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:17.950
I think this is better.

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:19.620
Oh, really?

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:23.910
Because if I lay down this way,
I can smell you.

00:06:23.910 --> 00:06:26.370
What?! Wait, do I have bad BO?

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:28.790
That's not what I meant.

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:32.120
Fine, I won't.

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:35.580
I think you lack elegance, Shimamura.

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:40.080
Elegance... Hm... Elegance, eh?

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:42.870
I don't think anyone's told me that before.

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:45.250
Say, Adachi.

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:49.450
Wanna actually go to class
with me this afternoon?

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:54.250
What brought that up?

00:06:54.250 --> 00:06:56.700
Well, you know, attendance and such...

00:06:56.700 --> 00:07:01.910
What I'm saying is, it'd be more fun if we both
made it as second-years together.

00:07:01.910 --> 00:07:03.330
Together...

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:06.080
I guess it wouldn't hurt once in a while.

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:07.870
Okay!

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:11.120
Then, hey... Let's go somewhere
once classes are over.

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:14.700
Did you have other plans?

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:16.250
Not today...

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:18.500
Actually, I never really do.

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:20.120
I see.

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:23.620
Maybe I'll actually get a bite today.

00:07:25.330 --> 00:07:30.200
School is its very own, unique society,

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:34.290
and if you brought that outside,
it confused things.

00:07:34.290 --> 00:07:40.950
So I'm sure that some people would just
prefer to live out their lives at school.

00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:44.870
That aside, I want to catch a bright future.

00:07:44.870 --> 00:07:48.750
And for that to happen, I've got to
cast my line, or nothing will begin.

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:51.620
How were your classes?

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:56.620
Japanese history was fine, but I definitely
don't understand math anymore.

00:07:57.500 --> 00:08:01.000
I've been to more classes than you and yet,
neither makes sense to me,

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:03.250
so where does that put me?

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:06.080
You seemed to get a lot of attention, Shimamura.

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:08.620
No, I'm pretty sure you did.

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:11.580
No, it was you.

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:14.000
It's probably because you're so pretty.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:15.660
Huh?

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:17.200
What's wrong?

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:21.200
Well, this is the first time
anyone's ever called me pretty, so...

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:25.580
Really? Your boy... friend
doesn't call you that?

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:27.830
I've never had one.

00:08:27.830 --> 00:08:32.950
Huh... I guess everyone must be blind.

00:08:32.950 --> 00:08:36.450
Huh? Wait, where's your bike?

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:38.040
It's out for repairs.

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:41.830
Huh... So you actually
walked to school. Good job.

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:44.330
Well, I thought you'd be here, so...

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:49.910
Oh, right...

00:08:57.080 --> 00:08:58.750
It's so sweet!

00:08:58.750 --> 00:09:02.250
Are you going to classes tomorrow, Shimamura?

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:06.700
Well, I'm going to at least do my best
to go for more than three days.

00:09:06.700 --> 00:09:08.290
I see.

00:09:09.370 --> 00:09:13.000
What do you say, Miss Adachi?
Why don't we put in a little effort together?

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:17.950
I guess... I can try a little harder.

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:21.660
Want a bite?

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:23.750
Sure. Ah...

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:33.450
Right back at you.

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:41.700
Adachi? Oh, I see.

00:09:43.330 --> 00:09:46.870
Here, there's some cream.
This is what you were waiting for, right?

00:09:46.870 --> 00:09:50.120
Oh, uh, sure...

00:09:56.160 --> 00:09:58.540
Where should we go after we eat?

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:02.700
Being with other people
seems to bring a little bit of pain.

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:05.290
Not understanding something.
Something being a pain.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:09.950
Trying to mend relationships.
Putting in effort to find solutions.

00:10:09.950 --> 00:10:10.950
But...

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:15.750
Sometimes a bit of happiness is rolling
around in between all that negativity.

00:10:15.750 --> 00:10:20.160
Just like when you're a kid and you find
a tiny ball that you thought you'd lost,

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:23.200
I want to believe that
the fact that I met Adachi

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:25.410
is going to bring me a brighter future.

00:10:53.450 --> 00:10:54.790
Um...

00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:58.330
If it's awkward, I'll let go! Like right away!

00:10:58.330 --> 00:11:01.200
It wasn't awkward. You just startled me.

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:02.700
Should I not then?

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:05.330
No, it's fine. Let's go.

00:11:05.330 --> 00:11:07.410
Do you like being coddled, Adachi?

00:11:07.410 --> 00:11:09.450
No...

00:11:09.450 --> 00:11:11.870
"Pedestrian-Vehicle Separated Signal"

00:11:09.450 --> 00:11:11.870
I'm sorta surprised.

00:11:11.870 --> 00:11:15.160
Well, I'm not...

00:11:15.160 --> 00:11:18.000
...that surprised...

00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:26.660
Shukoh... Shukoh...

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:28.080
Hello.

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:30.540
Oh, uh, hey...

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:33.410
I saw you here, so I thought I would say hi.

00:11:33.410 --> 00:11:36.660
You really just walk around
in front of the station in that...

00:11:36.660 --> 00:11:40.290
Well, this is my finest outfit.

00:11:40.290 --> 00:11:43.910
I smell something exquisitely sweet
from your fingers.

00:11:43.910 --> 00:11:47.580
Yes, this is quite nice. What is it?

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:52.700
Probably donuts, since I just ate some.

00:11:52.700 --> 00:11:54.700
Donuts?

00:11:57.290 --> 00:12:00.700
What are you doing?
Though I saw that coming...

00:12:00.700 --> 00:12:06.080
There was a blip on my radar!
There're donuts in there, aren't there?

00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:08.950
Yeah, but don't grab at it.

00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:12.000
If you give me one of those d-donuts,

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:16.620
I shall reveal one of
the secrets of the universe!

00:12:16.620 --> 00:12:20.750
Huh? This is for my little sister.

00:12:21.870 --> 00:12:24.750
--If they eat a donut, they'll take off
their helmet, and I can see their face.

00:12:24.750 --> 00:12:26.500
--Poik.
--If they eat a donut, they'll take off
their helmet, and I can see their face.

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:30.080
Okay, fine. You can have one.

00:12:31.330 --> 00:12:33.620
Let's see... You can have this one.

00:12:33.620 --> 00:12:36.410
Ah, so this is a donut.

00:12:38.700 --> 00:12:41.790
Squeak, squeak, squeak, squeak...

00:12:41.790 --> 00:12:43.580
Pshuu.

00:12:45.250 --> 00:12:47.500
--Munchy, munchy, munchy, munchy, munchy...

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:50.120
--You're not taking off your helmet?!
--Munchy, munchy, munchy, munchy, munchy...

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:53.290
Munchy... Gulp.

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:54.580
Plop.

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:57.790
--Yes, this was nice. It's very sweet!
It's oh so sweet!

00:12:57.790 --> 00:13:02.080
--You've never heard of donuts before?
What kind of dance is that?
--Yes, this was nice. It's very sweet!
It's oh so sweet!

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:04.500
Do you have any more sweets?

00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:05.790
Buy some yourself.

00:13:05.790 --> 00:13:07.750
I have no money.

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:09.040
How do you survive?

00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:10.160
Shimamura.

00:13:11.750 --> 00:13:13.120
I'm going to get my bike.

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:14.120
Huh?

00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:15.620
Later.

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:18.450
I'll see you tomorrow.

00:13:18.450 --> 00:13:21.200
Wait, was she mad?

00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:24.410
Would you like me to tell you what just happened

00:13:24.410 --> 00:13:26.450
instead of one of the universe's secrets?

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:27.580
Sure...

00:13:28.580 --> 00:13:31.700
She's mad because she didn't get a donut!

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:32.870
Go home.

00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:35.450
I have no idea if this self-proclaimed person

00:13:35.450 --> 00:13:40.540
from the future is going to
greatly change my life.

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:43.870
It's not like things usually change your life.

00:13:43.870 --> 00:13:46.200
Because no one knows what the future holds.

00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:48.750
You can't change it.

00:13:48.750 --> 00:13:52.700
Man, relationships are hard...

00:13:52.700 --> 00:13:54.290
I totally understand.

00:13:54.290 --> 00:13:55.870
Understand what?

00:13:58.910 --> 00:14:04.290
Apparently, Shimamura thinks
I'm prettier for some reason.

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:07.950
But she is greatly mistaken.

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:13.250
I'd say that Shimamura is way cuter.

00:14:13.250 --> 00:14:17.620
Her dreamy eyes, the way
she modestly moves her lips...

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:24.750
My eyes keep looking at her face,
especially her lips.

00:14:40.410 --> 00:14:43.750
I had a dream where I kissed Shimamura.

00:14:45.790 --> 00:14:49.040
It's not like I'm into that.

00:14:49.040 --> 00:14:53.790
I think I just want to be closer
with Shimamura...

00:14:53.790 --> 00:14:56.950
But it's definitely not like that.

00:14:56.950 --> 00:14:59.160
There's no deep meaning behind that kiss.

00:15:06.120 --> 00:15:08.080
Nope! None!

00:15:08.080 --> 00:15:10.910
I'm not saying I'd never kiss her...

00:15:10.910 --> 00:15:16.080
But I'm not saying I absolutely want to, either?

00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:20.450
If there was no one else within
a 5-kilometer radius from Shimamura,

00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:24.250
and she was in a deep sleep and an all-knowing
deity just happened to reassure me

00:15:24.250 --> 00:15:27.290
that she wasn't going to wake up
in the next 24 hours,

00:15:27.290 --> 00:15:29.870
maybe I'd get bored
after 23 hours and I might

00:15:29.870 --> 00:15:33.540
kiss her once to relieve some boredom...

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:37.080
Huh? Wait...

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:43.790
But I'm definitely not that.
I just want Shimamura to put me first.

00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:49.870
I want Shimamura to think of me first
when she hears the word "friend."

00:15:49.870 --> 00:15:55.160
I know that may sound a bit possessive...

00:15:55.160 --> 00:15:57.790
To be quite honest, I've been wondering

00:15:57.790 --> 00:16:02.580
how much of a friend
Shimamura actually sees me as.

00:16:02.580 --> 00:16:07.790
Am I just like her other friends?
Or does she have other feelings for me?

00:16:07.790 --> 00:16:09.790
"Sunday"

00:16:07.790 --> 00:16:09.790
Am I just like her other friends?
Or does she have other feelings for me?

00:16:12.330 --> 00:16:14.120
Welcom--

00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:17.200
Huh?

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:26.620
Ah...

00:16:28.540 --> 00:16:31.080
I told you it was embarrassing.

00:16:31.080 --> 00:16:33.000
It's fine. It suits you.

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:35.700
Ah, a friend.

00:16:35.700 --> 00:16:40.040
I don't see them much anymore at our house
since she entered high school.

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:41.500
Ah...

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:43.660
Really, don't worry about it.

00:16:43.660 --> 00:16:45.830
Oho... Are you two in the same class?

00:16:45.830 --> 00:16:47.160
Seriously.

00:16:47.160 --> 00:16:49.040
Oh, come on.

00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:51.700
Let's just order already.

00:16:51.700 --> 00:16:53.080
I'll have <i>tantanmen</i>.

00:16:53.080 --> 00:16:54.660
Then I'll have...

00:16:55.330 --> 00:16:59.330
Apparently, Shimamura
doesn't really understand me,

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:01.000
but I could say the same about her.

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:03.540
She doesn't push me away when I rely on her,

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:06.700
but she doesn't try to rely on anyone herself.

00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:10.410
That was how I saw Shimamura.

00:17:10.410 --> 00:17:14.040
I thought you were finally shaping up,
and now look at you.

00:17:15.830 --> 00:17:17.250
Who's that supposed to be?

00:17:17.250 --> 00:17:21.870
Our teacher. They were asking me
where you were like I'd be able to answer.

00:17:23.750 --> 00:17:25.200
What?

00:17:25.200 --> 00:17:28.660
I was just thinking about how cute
you looked yesterday.

00:17:28.660 --> 00:17:32.750
Huh? B-But you're cute, too, Shimamura...

00:17:32.750 --> 00:17:39.580
Huh? It's not like I did anything.
Maybe I'll go there to eat again.

00:17:39.580 --> 00:17:42.000
Don't. Please don't.

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:46.290
I'm kidding. I'm not sure if I want
to go again with my family...

00:17:47.410 --> 00:17:49.250
--It is sort of embarrassing
when you're with family--

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:51.950
--Hey, it's Shimamura!
--It is sort of embarrassing
when you're with family--

00:17:51.950 --> 00:17:55.540
Huh? Oh, so you did come.
Can I sit next to you?

00:17:55.540 --> 00:17:57.370
Uh, sure...

00:17:58.700 --> 00:18:02.790
Um... You're... Right?

00:18:02.790 --> 00:18:05.450
It's Adachi! Adachi.

00:18:05.450 --> 00:18:09.290
You forgot her name but somehow
really thought whispering would work?

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:13.540
So, Adachi.

00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:14.870
Good morning.

00:18:14.870 --> 00:18:16.830
G-Good morning.

00:18:16.830 --> 00:18:18.540
It's rare for you to eat school lunch.

00:18:18.540 --> 00:18:20.950
--I guess I don't hate this.
--Well my dear <i>maman </i>slept in today.

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:24.500
Their noisiness isn't bad.

00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:29.290
It reminded me of lunchtime in
grade school and was a bit nostalgic.

00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:35.330
But it also felt like they were cutting
into my time alone with Shimamura.

00:18:37.410 --> 00:18:43.290
I can't deny that I felt
that this didn't feel right.

00:18:45.200 --> 00:18:48.410
Adachi, what are you going
to do about the afternoon?

00:18:48.410 --> 00:18:51.580
Um... I plan to go to class... I think.

00:18:51.580 --> 00:18:52.620
I see.

00:18:54.290 --> 00:18:55.450
Shimamura...

00:18:57.620 --> 00:19:01.120
I was wondering if I...

00:19:01.120 --> 00:19:03.200
...could go to your house today.

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:08.410
This way.

00:19:08.410 --> 00:19:09.870
Okay...

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:14.450
Welcome home, Big... Sis.

00:19:14.450 --> 00:19:16.200
Hi...

00:19:16.200 --> 00:19:20.040
Thanks. Oh, this is my friend. From yesterday.

00:19:20.040 --> 00:19:21.290
Yeah...

00:19:25.500 --> 00:19:27.000
Sorry...

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:28.040
Oh, don't worry.

00:19:28.040 --> 00:19:30.040
She's a bit shy.

00:19:31.790 --> 00:19:33.750
So your room's on the first floor.

00:19:33.750 --> 00:19:35.080
Yeah.

00:19:35.080 --> 00:19:37.450
You can sit wherever.

00:19:37.450 --> 00:19:40.870
There we go.

00:19:40.870 --> 00:19:42.450
So, what should we do?

00:19:42.450 --> 00:19:44.160
Y-Yeah...

00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:56.540
Say, Shimamura...

00:19:56.540 --> 00:19:57.410
Hm?

00:19:57.410 --> 00:20:00.660
Don't say it, don't say it, don't say it...

00:20:00.660 --> 00:20:03.330
Um, do you mind if I sit...?

00:20:03.330 --> 00:20:04.950
Huh?

00:20:04.950 --> 00:20:08.870
Like... Between your legs...

00:20:08.870 --> 00:20:13.700
What did I just say?!
Oh, my God. I'm a complete weirdo.

00:20:13.700 --> 00:20:14.540
Sure.

00:20:14.540 --> 00:20:16.370
Wait, it's okay?!

00:20:17.910 --> 00:20:20.500
Wait, huh? I...

00:20:20.500 --> 00:20:21.750
It's okay?

00:20:21.750 --> 00:20:23.910
Is this a dream? Is it?

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:25.750
So it's okay?

00:20:25.750 --> 00:20:28.040
Shimamura's legs...

00:20:34.790 --> 00:20:36.950
What are you doing?

00:20:36.950 --> 00:20:39.370
Well, I mean...

00:20:39.370 --> 00:20:40.330
Huh?

00:20:40.330 --> 00:20:42.040
There!

00:20:42.040 --> 00:20:44.500
Huh? Hello?! What?!

00:20:44.500 --> 00:20:50.540
Hm? Well, my little sister likes
to sit like this. Isn't this normal?

00:20:50.540 --> 00:20:53.120
Y-Yeah, sure...

00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:54.120
--It's weird. It's super weird!
My clavicle hurts!

00:20:54.120 --> 00:20:55.750
--Um...
--It's weird. It's super weird!
My clavicle hurts!

00:20:55.750 --> 00:20:57.250
--What's up?
--It's weird. It's super weird!
My clavicle hurts!

00:20:57.250 --> 00:20:59.290
--Do you have a boyfriend?
--Usually, people feel pain in their chest,
but I'm feeling it in my bones.

00:20:59.290 --> 00:21:00.830
--Do you think I have one?
--Usually, people feel pain in their chest,
but I'm feeling it in my bones.

00:21:00.830 --> 00:21:02.000
--No...
--Usually, people feel pain in their chest,
but I'm feeling it in my bones.

00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:06.120
--You're right. Actually,
I told you that the other day.
--My bones start grinding so much
that it feels like they're out in the open.

00:21:06.120 --> 00:21:07.540
--Did you?
--My bones start grinding so much
that it feels like they're out in the open.

00:21:07.540 --> 00:21:09.950
--Do you have one, Adachi?
--I just want to relax...

00:21:09.950 --> 00:21:11.200
I don't...

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:13.000
I see.

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:15.830
And I immediately figured out

00:21:15.830 --> 00:21:17.700
how to do that.

00:21:19.450 --> 00:21:21.700
I like... you, I think...

00:21:21.700 --> 00:21:28.790
Wait, what?! What did I just try to say?
Did I say it? Wait, did I?!

00:21:30.410 --> 00:21:34.410
I think... I like you, Shimamura.

00:21:34.410 --> 00:21:37.830
Nope, I'm done for.
I can't... I'm an idiot.

00:21:37.830 --> 00:21:41.120
This is... This is... This is...

00:21:41.120 --> 00:21:46.700
I-I think I like you... Possibly, maybe...

00:21:46.700 --> 00:21:49.540
You know, like... really like...

00:21:49.540 --> 00:21:52.000
I'm a complete moron...

00:21:57.660 --> 00:22:03.080
Um... You okay? Are you breathing?
Your face is like bright red...

00:22:12.450 --> 00:22:14.950
What the efffffff...

00:22:16.910 --> 00:22:20.870
What the efffffff?!

00:22:20.870 --> 00:22:22.500
"Episode 2: Adachi Question"

00:22:20.870 --> 00:22:22.500
--Ow! Ow, ow... My neck hurts. It hurts.

00:22:22.500 --> 00:22:25.040
"Episode 2: Adachi Question"

00:22:22.500 --> 00:22:25.040
--Ow! Ow, ow... My neck hurts. It hurts.
--Even if the sun were to set and rise again,

00:22:25.040 --> 00:22:27.950
"Episode 2: Adachi Question"

00:22:25.040 --> 00:22:27.950
would tomorrow even come for me?

